        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.595,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Parallel and Intersecting Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.846,
            0.138
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "5.4 Parallel and Perpendicular Lines in Paper Folding"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.147,
            0.259,
            0.168
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.166,
            0.841,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": "Take a plain square sheet of paper (use a newspaper for this activity)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.19,
            0.846,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "• How would you describe the opposite edges of the sheet? They are to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.232,
            0.847,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "How would you describe the adjacent edges of the sheet? The adjacent edges are to each other. They meet at a point. They form right angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.294,
            0.846,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": "• Fold the sheet horizontally in half. A new line is formed (see Fig. 5.7)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.336,
            0.848,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": "How many parallel lines do you see now? How does the new line segment relate to the vertical sides?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.313,
            0.571,
            0.376,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.395,
            0.599,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.474,
                0.705,
                0.54,
                0.719
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.7"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.731,
            0.846,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "Make one more horizontal fold in the folded sheet. How many parallel lines do you see now?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.773,
            0.847,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "What will happen if you do it once more? How many parallel lines will you get? Is there a pattern? Check if the pattern extends further, if you make another horizontal fold."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.834,
            0.847,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "• Make a vertical fold in the square sheet. This new vertical line is to the previous horizontal lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.877,
            0.847,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": "• Fold the sheet along a diagonal. Can you find a fold that creates a line parallel to the diagonal line?"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
